# RAMYA-COOK environment variables
#
# The MVP needs NO environment variables — search, timers, the cooking engine,
# recommendations, favorites, history, pantry and the shopping list all run
# client-side with local persistence (Vercel free-tier friendly).
#
# These are placeholders for FUTURE server-side features. Secrets must live only
# on the server (a Vercel Serverless/Edge function), never in client code.
# Anything exposed to the browser must be prefixed VITE_ — never put a secret there.

# --- Future: RAMYA AI Chef via a secure server endpoint ---
# The browser calls /api/chef; the function reads this key server-side.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Future: database-backed sync (optional) ---
# DATABASE_URL=

# --- Public site URL (used for canonical URLs / sitemap if set) ---
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://ramya-cook.example.com
